('d-rcc-originals-predate-curriqunet-s666','decision','Riverside City 30578 and 33829 keep their current records; originals predate curriQunet','S666: the archive 7 (2024-2025) prior read (run 43889274787, $0.078, no PR) matched 33829 to a page titled Business Administration 2.0 (fails coverage) and found no page for 30578 (near miss, 1 of 14 codes). Both current records stay; the plain originals sit in rcc.edu''s 2023-2024 or older PDF catalogs, which the curriQunet-only prior route cannot read.',array['program-requirements-harvest','riverside-city','decision'],'proposed','S666 checkpoint; docs/session_667_handoff.md and the lane files',null,null,'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16'),
('d-mpc-reload-three-s666','decision','Monterey Peninsula 03653, 22098, 39361 reloaded insert-only','S666: three Monterey Peninsula programs Active in COCI had no live program_requirement_records row since 2026-11-09 and no deletion receipt. step=load run 43892853333 (insert-only) inserted 3 and kept 197; receipt kb/receipts/program_requirement_records_college_monterey_peninsula_43892853333.json; draft #3399. The next display build carries them.',array['program-requirements-harvest','monterey-peninsula','decision'],'proposed','S666 checkpoint; docs/session_667_handoff.md and the lane files',null,null,'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16'),
('d-honors-step2-applied-not-a-hold-s666','decision','Honors step 2 applied: Sheet 200 card 1 was not a hold under the ask test','S666, on the ask test (Sam, 2026-11-16, relayed by COBIx on #3358): the check reran (380 rows, digest 29667c0741e7e7fafb509b4c2937e9db) and supabase-migrate.yml run 43889173474 inserted 380 honors_of rows under honors-rows-s653@bot (#3397, 32d69d90). Rollback kb/migrations/2026-11-14_s653_honors_of_rows_rollback.sql, by cohort. Answers Sheet 200 card 1.',array['commons','honors','reclustering','decision'],'proposed','S666 checkpoint; docs/session_667_handoff.md and the lane files',null,null,'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16'),
('d-person-saved-never-returns-s666','decision','Another look never proposes a move away from a person''s save','S666, #3396 (b460ea57): all 6 cards of the Nov 13 Another look sweep were Sam''s own saves. kb/_sweep_exhibit_titles.py person_saved() drops a move whose current title is a person''s overlay save (a bot cohort''s save still gets a card); _fold_unclassified.py''s revise lane needs a person''s row to supersede a human-reviewed title. Sweep 6 cards to 0.',array['cer-procedures','exhibits','curation','decision'],'proposed','S666 checkpoint; docs/session_667_handoff.md and the lane files',null,null,'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16'),
('p-prior-rescore-route-is-prior-plus-reconcile-s666','procedure','Rescore a prior-catalog read for free: a prior dispatch with step=reconcile','S666: sources_from=<prior run> is refused, because stage_sources accepts only capture.json or capture_preview.json accounts, never prior_<year>.json. The free route to rescore a prior read is a program-requirements-college.yml prior dispatch with step=reconcile (no model call); its log carries calgetc_trace. Run 43880453260 held Physics 32745 (28 + 34 = 62).',array['program-requirements-harvest','prior-catalog','procedure'],'proposed','S666 checkpoint; docs/session_667_handoff.md and the lane files',null,null,'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16'),
('p-dependency-map-reads-committed-files-s666','pitfall','The dependency map reads committed files: regenerate after the commit','S666: kb/_build_dependency_map.py reads committed files, so docs/reference/dependency_map.md goes stale after any commit that adds a file, and scripts/check_generated.sh then fails. Commit first, run the builder, and commit the regenerated map (as #3396 did).',array['ci','dependency-map','pitfall'],'proposed','S666 checkpoint; docs/session_667_handoff.md and the lane files',null,null,'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16'),
('sam-sql-prompt-is-app-level-2026-11-16','fact','Sam: the Supabase connector is on Always allow; the Execute SQL prompt is the app''s','Sam, in session, 2026-11-16, verbatim: "it is set that way and has been for some time" (the claude.ai Supabase connector is on Always allow). The per-call Execute SQL prompt still appears; no repo setting clears it (session root settings, the guard hook and the connector all allow). Check writes by the runner''s committed receipt and batch reads.',array['governance','supabase','permissions','fact'],'verified','Sam, in session S666, 2026-11-16','Sam Lee',now(),'SkyDipper (S666)',date '2026-11-16')
